# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in — or let `bash scripts/setup-board.sh` do it for you.
# Never commit the real values: the conformance check scans every pull request for credentials,
# but it fires after the push — a committed key is burned and must be rotated first, then removed
# (CONTRIBUTING.md). Where each value comes from is `docs/credentials.md`.

# The CTFd board the Solver plays. This one value decides which competition it enters, so it is
# the guard against pointing a permitted-AI agent at a no-AI platform.
#   BrunnerCTF Global (AI permitted): https://global.brunnerctf.dk
#   BrunnerCTF Denmark — strict no-AI, never point the Solver here.
CTFD_URL=

# A CTFd access token minted on that board: Settings -> Access Tokens -> Generate.
# Shown once. It carries the account's full privileges, so it is per-board and revocable.
CTFD_API_TOKEN=

# The IN-CYPHER team key. It identifies and gates this team on the competition platform —
# including the proof-of-work gate on raw-TCP challenges — and must stay within the team.
# Issued by the organisers; not needed for practice boards like Brunner.
TEAM_KEY=

# How the Solver pays for inference. Any LLM is allowed, and we hold subscriptions to more
# than one, so this is per provider rather than a single key. Practice runs go on a
# subscription — no per-token cost, a quota that hard-stops until it resets. The scored run
# goes on metered billing, which costs money and has no cliff to fall off mid-run.
#
# ONE credential per provider. An empty value is not an unset one: the variable occupies its
# slot in the client's credential search the moment it exists, so a leftover
# `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` shadows a token and authenticates with nothing — and `docker run
# --env-file` exports empty values, so the container fails while this file still looks right.
# Delete the lines you are not using rather than blanking them.

# Anthropic — subscription. `sk-ant-oat01-…`, minted by `claude setup-token`. Use
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN when the Solver drives Claude Code or the Agent SDK; use
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN when it calls the Messages API directly. Either way the token rides
# `Authorization: Bearer` — putting it in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY sends `x-api-key` and fails auth.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Anthropic — metered. `sk-ant-api03-…` from console.anthropic.com. Never set alongside a
# token: the SDK sends both headers and the API rejects the request outright.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI / Codex — metered. `sk-…` from platform.openai.com.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI / Codex — subscription. Codex does NOT read a token from the environment: it stores
# credentials in ~/.codex/auth.json, so a container is authenticated by piping the token in
# (`codex login --with-access-token`) or by `codex login --device-auth`, not by an env var
# alone. This value is the material for that pipe. See docs/credentials.md.
# CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN=
